<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Tolbert</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1913">1913</a>–<a href="/years/1980">1980</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as William R. Tolbert Jr.</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Tolbert was the 20th president of Liberia, serving from 1971, when he succeeded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-tubman">William Tubman</a>, until 1980. Leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/true-whig-party">True Whig Party</a>, he faced growing opposition, and a proposed rise in the price of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> led to deadly riots in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monrovia">Monrovia</a> in April 1979. He was killed in the military coup of 12 April 1980 led by Master Sergeant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-doe">Samuel Doe</a>, which ended more than a century of True Whig rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-tolbert.jpg" alt="William Tolbert" width="320" height="535" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kightlinger, Jack E., Photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_R._Tolbert,_Jr..JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
